common-midpoint-three-rank-arithmetic-co.statement:
Retain the full canonical hard common-midpoint cross family and the notation of `common-midpoint-upstream-three-rank-ledger`: its mass \(M>7Q/800\), reflected-cloud affine rank \(k_c\), original-parent centroid ranks \((\rho_{\mathrm{cen}},r_{\mathrm{cen}})\), and original-contact ranks \((\rho_{\mathrm{par}},r_{\mathrm{par}})\).  Assume every label-containing leaf-distinct quotient-full-rank star meeting the family satisfies \(\mathcal B_\eta<Q/(200\gamma_d)\).  Prove

\[
\max\left\{
4\gamma_{2d}2^n\frac{M}{k_c+1},
2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{cen}}}\frac{2M}{r_{\mathrm{cen}}+1},
4\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{par}}}\frac{M}{r_{\mathrm{par}}+1}
\right\}
\ge\frac Q{100}.
\]

pk-intake-actual-positive-ray-projective.statement:
There is a compact full-dimensional convex body $C\subset\mathbb R\times\mathbb R^2$ with positive-area integer fibers exactly at $0,1,2$, and an anchor $(0,x_0)\in C$ with $x_0$ in the interior of its fiber, for which the normalized positive-ray projective shadow satisfies
$$
\inf\{\mu(H):H\subset\mathbb R^2\text{ a closed halfspace},\ y\in H\}
\ \le\ \frac{458329}{1040000}
\ =\ \frac49-\frac{35039}{9360000}
\qquad\text{for every }y\in\mathbb R^2.
$$
Here $\mu$ is the probability measure obtained by summing the pushforwards of planar area on the positive integer fibers $K_k=\{x:(k,x)\in C\}$ under $x\mapsto (x-x_0)/k$, then dividing by the sum of their areas. Its density is quasiconcave. Thus even this class of actual convex-body shadows need not have a point of depth $4/9$.

pk-intake-ambient-simplex-projective-pro.statement:
Let $C\subset\mathbb R\times\mathbb R^d$ be a full-dimensional $(d+1)$-simplex of ambient volume $V$, $d\ge1$, $m=d+1$, with vertex heights $h_i$. At an interior non-knot height $s$ let $I=\{i:h_i<s\}$, $J=\{j:h_j>s\}$, $\delta_i=|h_i-s|$. For $\alpha\in\Delta_{|I|-1}$ and $\beta\in\Delta_{|J|-1}$ write $L=\sum_{i\in I}\alpha_i/\delta_i+\sum_{j\in J}\beta_j/\delta_j$. The section is parametrized in barycentrics by $\lambda_i=\alpha_i/(\delta_i L)$ for $i\in I$ and $\lambda_j=\beta_j/(\delta_j L)$ for $j\in J$. For an ambient affine functional with vertex values $a_i$, the $d$-volume of its closed upper cap at threshold $b$ on this section is
$$
\frac{m!V}{\prod_i\delta_i}
\int_{\Delta_{|I|-1}\times\Delta_{|J|-1}}
\mathbf 1\!\left\{\sum_{i\in I}\frac{(a_i-b)\alpha_i}{\delta_i}
+\sum_{j\in J}\frac{(a_j-b)\beta_j}{\delta_j}\ge0\right\} L^{-m}\,d\alpha\,d\beta .
$$
The simplex measures here are coordinate Lebesgue measures of total masses $1/(|I|-1)!$ and $1/(|J|-1)!$, with mass one in dimension zero. Dropping the indicator gives the whole slice volume $w(s)$. For nonvertical caps use continuous limits at interior knots and inward limits at endpoints. For vertical caps use $w(s)$ times the exact closed base indicator, including at knots and endpoints. The sum over the original integer heights is the raw mixed mass.

pk-intake-present-corner-same-cut-chord-.statement:
Let $A,K,B$ be planar convex bodies with $K$ a triangle. Let $y\in\operatorname{int}K$ and let $v_1,v_2,v_3$ be nonzero spanning normals with $\sum_i v_i=0$. The three middle caps $v_i\cdot(x-y)\ge0$ strictly capture distinct vertices $P_i$ of $K$ and strictly exclude the other two vertices. Put $k=|K|$, $a=|A|$, $\beta=|B|/k$, $h_i=h_B(v_i)-v_i\cdot y$, $W=\sum_i h_i$, $D=|\det(v_1,v_2)|$, $H=\sum_i v_i\cdot(P_i-y)$, and $R=8Dk/H^2$. Let $q_i$ be the middle cap fractions, $f_i=2v_i\cdot(P_i-y)/(H\sqrt{q_i})$, and $U_i$ the area of the $A$ cap $v_i\cdot(x-y)\ge-h_i$. Denote the lengths of the cutting chords in $A$ and $K$, divided by $\lVert v_i\rVert$, by $\sigma_{A,i}$ and $\sigma_{K,i}$.

The support triangle $\{x:v_i\cdot(x-y)\le h_i \text{ for every }i\}$ contains $B$, has area $W^2/(2D)$, and gives $H/W\le2/\sqrt{\beta R}$. For an index $i$ with a proper $A$ cut and a nonempty residual corner $A\cap\bigcap_{j\ne i}\{x:v_j\cdot(x-y)<-h_j\}$, put $T_i=|A\cap\{x:v_i\cdot(x-y)\ge W-h_i\}|$ and $\delta_i=(a-U_j-U_k)_+$, with the other indices $j,k$. Then
$$
\frac{\sigma_{A,i}}{\sigma_{K,i}}
\le \frac{f_i}{\sqrt{q_i}\sqrt{\beta R}}\frac{U_i}{k}
       \left(1-\sqrt{T_i/U_i}\right)
\le \frac{f_i}{\sqrt{q_i}\sqrt{\beta R}}\frac{U_i}{k}
       \left(1-\sqrt{\delta_i/U_i}\right).
$$
If all budgets $U_i+kq_i=Q$ agree, these terms satisfy $U_i/k=Q/k-q_i$ and $\delta_i/k=(a/k-(Q/k-q_j)-(Q/k-q_k))_+$.

pk-intake-regular-singleton-density-affi.statement:
Use the accepted exact energy-only regular buffered cover continuation on a finite lattice-complete positive compatible family. Let $M=\sum_z|K_z|$, $Q=\beta M$ be its old raw buffered maximum, $N=d+1$, $\Sigma$ the old within-fiber covariance, and $g_z$ the ordinary centroid of $K_z$. For group $i$, let the positive weights $\rho_{ij}$ sum to one and the selected continuous covectors satisfy $u_{ij}^{\mathsf T}\Sigma u_{ij}=1$. Write $S_{ij}>0$ for the mixed coarea of its proper sections, $B_i=\sum_j\rho_{ij}/S_{ij}$, and $\theta_{ij}=(\rho_{ij}/S_{ij})/B_i$. Assume every chosen cap has only proper, strict full or empty, or zero-surface-area supporting traces, with a proper own trace. The assigned contact faces are then singletons, with at most $k(P)\le 2^n$ groups. Denote the source by $(p_i,y_i)$, its own projective optimizer by $a_i$, $P_i(X)=1+a_i\cdot(X-y_i)$ on $K_{p_i}$, and its energy by $E_i$. Put $\delta_i=\varepsilon(E_i/M)^{1/N}/B_i$, where $\varepsilon>0$. For any fixed real dual weights $\eta_i$ define
$$
\begin{aligned}
W_i(z,X)&=\sum_j\theta_{ij}\kappa_{ij}(z,X),\\
\Xi_z(X)&=\sum_i\eta_i\left[W_i(z,X)-\beta+
\delta_i\left(\frac{\mathbf1_{z=p_i}P_i(X)^{-N}}{NE_i}
+\frac{\sum_j\rho_{ij}[u_{ij}\cdot(X-g_z)]^2}{2M}
-\frac{N+2}{2NM}\right)\right],
\end{aligned}
$$
where $\kappa_{ij}$ is the physical regular fixed-cap selector and the projective term is used only when $z=p_i$. For any actual bounded signed radial speed $v$, the corresponding linear combination of the normalized budget decrease coefficients multiplied by $M$ is $\sum_z\int_{\partial K_z}\Xi_zv_z\,dS$. Each individual group coefficient vanishes on $v_z(X)=-n_z(X)\cdot(A X+Bz+c)$ for arbitrary common $A,B,c$, where $n_z$ is the old outward unit normal.

root-affine-simplex-filling.statement:
Let \(\Delta=\operatorname{conv}\{v_0,\ldots,v_q\}\) be a lattice simplex whose vertices lie in the canonical stopped set \(A_\star\), and let \(\lambda_0,\ldots,\lambda_q\) be its barycentric-coordinate functions. Prove the exact physical root-affine filling inequality

\[
G_{\operatorname{aff}\Delta}^{\mathrm{rel}}
\ge
4\sum_{z\in\Delta\cap\mathbb Z^n}
\left(
\sum_{i=0}^q\lambda_i(z)w_{v_i}^{1/d}
\right)^d
\]

when \(q<n\), and the analogous global \(G\)-bound when \(q=n\). The proof must construct positive feasible masses at every lattice point of \(\Delta\), one affine field of actual metronoid points, an integral centerpoint, and one point common to all barycentric Minkowski sums. It must use exact positive-mass convexity, not only closure.

support-safe-pair-energy.success_criterion:
A positive packet must prove the support-safe depth inequality for arbitrary pairwise disjoint symmetric pairs. It must:

- solve the two-variable capped maximization exactly for every \(d\geq1\), including \(S_0\geq A+B\);
- keep the positive-support and support-loss cases separate;
- handle vertical, nonvertical, boundary-through-point, and whole-space halfspaces;
- avoid extending a cap-volume root profile by zero outside its positive support;
- show how the result compares with and genuinely strengthens `92b530e0a2281d6e`;
- give an exact compact full-dimensional convex-body family showing that deleting the support-safe truncation makes the claimed universal energy false, or else rigorously refute that proposed calibration.

A negative packet must give an exact compact full-dimensional convex body satisfying the hypotheses and compute a halfspace through \((z_0,x_0)\) whose mixed mass is smaller than the registered support-safe right-hand side. A counterexample only to the untruncated consultation formula is an obstacle/calibration, not a disproof of the registered theorem.
